Relevant columns and how they will be used

sales.prod_id: identify the product that was sold  
sales.cust_id: link each sale to the customer who made it  
sales.time_id: link each sale to a date in the times table in order to know the quarter (calendar_quarter_id)  
sales.channel_id: not needed here  
sales.promo_id: filter on promo_id = 999  
sales.quantity_sold / sales.amount_sold: measure of city‑level and product‑level sales  

customers.cust_id: joins to sales  
customers.country_id: joins to countries so we can keep only United‑States customers  
customers.cust_city: city whose growth we must analyse  

countries.country_id: joins to customers  
countries.country_name = 'United States' → condition that limits the analysis to U.S. sales only  

times.time_id: joins to sales  
times.calendar_quarter_id: filter on quarter 1772 (Q4‑2019) or 1776 (Q4‑2020)  

products.prod_id: joins to sales  
products.prod_name: the human‑readable product name to show in the result  

Filter conditions that will be used

• sales.promo_id = 999  
• countries.country_name = 'United States'  
• times.calendar_quarter_id IN (1772, 1776)  
• City growth condition (later):  
     SUM(amount_sold_Q4‑2020) >= 1.20 × SUM(amount_sold_Q4‑2019)  

Below are ten exploratory / building‑block SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that progress from simple inspection to an almost‑complete answer.  
All queries are written for SQLite; they use double quotes for identifiers and a LIMIT 20.

```sql
-- 1.  Find the country_id that corresponds to the United States
SELECT DISTINCT "country_id", "country_name"
FROM "countries"
WHERE "country_name" = 'United States'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2.  List a sample of U.S. customers with their city
SELECT DISTINCT c."cust_id", c."cust_city"
FROM "customers" AS c
JOIN "countries" AS co
  ON c."country_id" = co."country_id"
WHERE co."country_name" = 'United States'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3.  Pick 20 sales rows in Q4‑2019 (calendar_quarter_id = 1772) with promo_id = 999
SELECT s.*, t."calendar_quarter_id"
FROM "sales" AS s
JOIN "times"  AS t  ON s."time_id" = t."time_id"
JOIN "customers" AS cu ON s."cust_id" = cu."cust_id"
JOIN "countries" AS co ON cu."country_id" = co."country_id"
WHERE co."country_name" = 'United States'
  AND s."promo_id" = 999
  AND t."calendar_quarter_id" = 1772
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
